    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0395" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.1281/85: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-03T17:00:00+01:00">August 3, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>372. The D. N. B.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d309-f1"/> reports the enactment of an
                    ordinance (not yet Promulgated) canceling as of September 30 of this year the
                    licenses <pb facs="0396" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/> to practice of all Jewish
                    physicians. It is not yet clear how this affects their possible practice among
                    other Jews<anchor n="47" xml:id="d309-f2"/> or foreigners.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d309-f1" n="46" xml:id="d309-f1-content">
                <p>Deutsches Nachrichten Büro.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d309-f2" n="47" xml:id="d309-f2-content">
                <p>From the text of law promulgated on August 4, it appeared that a limited number
                    of Jewish physicians would be permitted to practice among Jewish patients.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
